# ---------- what does not belong in the repository ----------
# The soundtrack and the effects: 400+ MB of recordings, and they are the originals' - they stay on this machine.
# Without them the game plays silently; copy audio/ into a clone by hand to get the music back.
audio/

# The reference rips the maps and sprites were drawn from (screenshots of the original games), and the generated
# art export - the game draws its own tiles in code (ART_MODE classic), so none of this is needed to play.
assets/
assets_backup/
art/
psynergy/
scenery/
prompts/
text/
map references/
reference images/
reference game mechanics/
battle references/
backgrounds references/

# The runner's own output: screenshots of every area, audit dumps, and the checkpoints of a playthrough in progress.
# The runner itself (runner/*.js and the plans) is kept.
runner/shots/
runner/*.txt
runner/ckpt_*.json
runner/report.json
runner/*.json.bak
runner/reveal_shot/
runner/ckpt_old/

# Tool data: the tile classifier's training set and the per-map working folders.
tools/__pycache__/
tools/tiletrain.npz
tools/tm/
tools/area_ref/
tools/caves/
tools/dungeons/
tools/towns/

# Scratch
*.pyc
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# The reference art archives dropped in at the root (psynergy.zip, battle.zip, ...): rips, like the folders above.
*.zip
